within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.N_NervousSystem.N01A_AnestheticsGeneral.N01AX10_Propofol;
model Propofol_Su2022_PD_sv
  "emax exposure-response sweep — Su_2022 :: SV (Stroke volume)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 8.04e-05,      // [m3; ml × 1e-06]
    Emax = -2.4e-07,  // [m3; ml × 1e-06]
    EC50 = 0.34,  // [kg/m3; mg ml À1 × 1]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 1);   // 1 mg ml À1 per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 3.4, Interval = 0.0068),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Propofol_Su2022_PD_sv</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Su H et al., <i>British journal of anaesthesia 128(5):806–816</i> 2022 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bja.2022.01.022\">doi:10.1016/j.bja.2022.01.022</a>) — Stroke volume [ml] against propofol mg ml À1 — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       80.4 ml       drug-free response (baseline) (Base SV, Q324)
  Emax  =      -0.24 ml       maximal effect term (E max_SV, Q323)
  EC50  =       0.34 mg ml À1 exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC 50 SV, Q321)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one mg ml À1 of propofol per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 8.04e-05   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (0.34 mg ml À1)  response 8.028e-05
  exposure -> infinity  response 8.016e-05</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Su_2022: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Propofol_Su2022_PD_sv;
